meta {
  name: Lucky Draws
  seq: 9
}

auth {
  mode: none
}

script:pre-request {
  bru.deleteVar("drawGroupId");
  bru.deleteVar("drawId");
}

docs {
  # Lucky Draws

  All routes require a valid Bearer access token, an ACTIVE account and active membership in the specified group. Every active member can see the shared draft and completed results. Only the creator may edit; every active member may run. Group owners and admins do not override creator-only editing. An inactive group allows reads but rejects Create, Update and Run.

  A group has at most one non-deleted DRAFT. Completing it makes room for the next draft. There is no delete, cancel, reset or rerun-for-a-new-result route. A repeat Run returns the same stored result. Concurrent Create is guarded by a unique PostgreSQL index; Update and Run lock the same draw row.

  Candidates have type, value and weight. TEXT value is a trimmed non-empty string of at most 255 characters. USER value is a positive JSON integer user ID, not a group member ID. USER candidates must be active accounts and active group members when creating or editing. User IDs are stored without a name or avatar snapshot. Fetch current names and avatars from GET /api/v1/users/{userID}/profile; cache by user ID within the page. A deleted/inactive account returns USER_NOT_FOUND; show a placeholder. Leaving the group later does not change an already-saved option or its chance automatically.

  WEIGHTED requires a weight on each option: greater than 0, at most 100, at most two decimal places, with a total of exactly 100. Values are JSON numbers such as 12.50, not strings with a % sign. Strings, exponent notation and more than two decimal places are rejected during binding. EQUAL assigns uniform actual odds. Omit weights for EQUAL; if supplied, they must match the automatic display allocation. Display percentages use 0.01 increments and total 100 (three equal options display 33.34, 33.33, 33.33); random selection remains exactly uniform in EQUAL mode.

  Duplicate TEXT values are rejected after trimming/case normalization; duplicate USER IDs are rejected. Different users sharing a name remain separate options. TEXT and USER are separate namespaces. There must be 2 to 100 options. Percentages are calculated with integer hundredths internally.

  Set drawGroupId and drawId manually in the selected environment. These requests do not automatically overwrite IDs. Login/Refresh keep their existing token scripts. Run the migrations before starting this backend version.
}
